Absolutely. Here’s a simple “Which Pokémon are you?” web app you can run locally. It asks a few personality questions, calculates a score, and shows a Pokémon-style result.

This version uses plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, so you do not need React, a backend, or a database.

## `index.html`

Create a file called `index.html` and paste this in:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Which Pokémon Are You?</title>
  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffcb05, #3b4cca);
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 24px;
      color: #222;
    }

    .app {
      background: white;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 650px;
      border-radius: 24px;
      padding: 32px;
      box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
      text-align: center;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-top: 0;
      color: #3b4cca;
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .subtitle {
      color: #555;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }

    .question {
      text-align: left;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      padding: 18px;
      border: 2px solid #eee;
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: #fafafa;
    }

    .question h2 {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    label {
      display: block;
      margin: 10px 0;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    input {
      margin-right: 8px;
    }

    button {
      background: #ffcb05;
      border: none;
      color: #2a2a2a;
      padding: 14px 24px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      cursor: pointer;
      box-shadow: 0 5px 0 #c7a000;
      transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
    }

    button:hover {
      transform: translateY(2px);
      box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #c7a000;
    }

    .result {
      display: none;
      margin-top: 28px;
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: #f4f7ff;
      border: 2px solid #d6ddff;
    }

    .pokemon-name {
      font-size: 2rem;
      color: #3b4cca;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .emoji {
      font-size: 4rem;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .error {
      color: #cc0000;
      font-weight: bold;
      margin-top: 12px;
      display: none;
    }

    .reset {
      margin-top: 18px;
      background: #3b4cca;
      color: white;
      box-shadow: 0 5px 0 #243080;
    }

    .reset:hover {
      box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #243080;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="app">
    <h1>Which Pokémon Are You?</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Answer a few questions and discover your inner Pokémon.</p>

    <form id="quizForm">
      <div class="question">
        <h2>1. What sounds most like you?</h2>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" value="pikachu" />
          Energetic, friendly, and a little chaotic
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" value="bulbasaur" />
          Calm, loyal, and grounded
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" value="charmander" />
          Passionate, bold, and adventurous
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" value="squirtle" />
          Cool, witty, and confident
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <h2>2. Your ideal weekend is...</h2>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" value="snorlax" />
          Sleeping, snacking, and doing absolutely nothing
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" value="eevee" />
          Trying something new
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" value="jigglypuff" />
          Singing, dancing, or entertaining friends
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" value="mewtwo" />
          Quiet time to think deeply
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <h2>3. In a group project, you are usually...</h2>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" value="pikachu" />
          The motivator
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" value="bulbasaur" />
          The reliable planner
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" value="charmander" />
          The one with big ideas
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" value="squirtle" />
          The problem solver
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <h2>4. Pick a power.</h2>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" value="pikachu" />
          Lightning speed
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" value="bulbasaur" />
          Healing nature energy
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" value="charmander" />
          Fire breath
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" value="mewtwo" />
          Mind control
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <h2>5. What do people appreciate about you?</h2>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" value="eevee" />
          I adapt to anything
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" value="snorlax" />
          I make people feel relaxed
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" value="jigglypuff" />
          I bring the fun
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" value="squirtle" />
          I stay cool under pressure
        </label>
      </div>

      <button type="submit">Reveal My Pokémon</button>
      <p class="error" id="error">Please answer every question first.</p>
    </form>

    <section class="result" id="result">
      <div class="emoji" id="pokemonEmoji"></div>
      <div class="pokemon-name" id="pokemonName"></div>
      <p id="pokemonDescription"></p>
      <button class="reset" id="resetButton">Take Quiz Again</button>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const pokemonResults = {
      pikachu: {
        name: "Pikachu",
        emoji: "⚡",
        description:
          "You are bright, energetic, and impossible to ignore. People love your spark, even when you are causing a little trouble."
      },
      bulbasaur: {
        name: "Bulbasaur",
        emoji: "🌱",
        description:
          "You are dependable, calm, and secretly powerful. You bring balance to the people around you."
      },
      charmander: {
        name: "Charmander",
        emoji: "🔥",
        description:
          "You are bold, passionate, and driven by excitement. When you care about something, your fire is unstoppable."
      },
      squirtle: {
        name: "Squirtle",
        emoji: "💧",
        description:
          "You are cool, clever, and charming. You know how to stay calm while still having fun."
      },
      eevee: {
        name: "Eevee",
        emoji: "✨",
        description:
          "You are adaptable, curious, and full of potential. You can become almost anything you want."
      },
      snorlax: {
        name: "Snorlax",
        emoji: "😴",
        description:
          "You are peaceful, comforting, and deeply committed to rest. Honestly? Iconic behavior."
      },
      jigglypuff: {
        name: "Jigglypuff",
        emoji: "🎤",
        description:
          "You are expressive, playful, and a natural performer. You bring drama, music, and personality everywhere."
      },
      mewtwo: {
        name: "Mewtwo",
        emoji: "🧠",
        description:
          "You are intense, thoughtful, and mysterious. You see things others miss and probably need more alone time."
      }
    };

    const form = document.getElementById("quizForm");
    const error = document.getElementById("error");
    const result = document.getElementById("result");
    const pokemonEmoji = document.getElementById("pokemonEmoji");
    const pokemonName = document.getElementById("pokemonName");
    const pokemonDescription = document.getElementById("pokemonDescription");
    const resetButton = document.getElementById("resetButton");

    form.addEventListener("submit", function (event) {
      event.preventDefault();

      const formData = new FormData(form);
      const answers = ["q1", "q2", "q3", "q4", "q5"];

      const scores = {};

      for (const question of answers) {
        const answer = formData.get(question);

        if (!answer) {
          error.style.display = "block";
          result.style.display = "none";
          return;
        }

        scores[answer] = (scores[answer] || 0) + 1;
      }

      error.style.display = "none";

      let topPokemon = null;
      let topScore = 0;

      for (const pokemon in scores) {
        if (scores[pokemon] > topScore) {
          topPokemon = pokemon;
          topScore = scores[pokemon];
        }
      }

      const finalResult = pokemonResults[topPokemon];

      pokemonEmoji.textContent = finalResult.emoji;
      pokemonName.textContent = finalResult.name;
      pokemonDescription.textContent = finalResult.description;

      result.style.display = "block";
      result.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth" });
    });

    resetButton.addEventListener("click", function () {
      form.reset();
      result.style.display = "none";
      error.style.display = "none";
      window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: "smooth" });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

## How to run it

Save the file as `index.html`, then double-click it. It should open in your browser.

## What it does

The quiz gives each answer a Pokémon value. At the end, it counts which Pokémon got the most points and displays that result.

## Easy upgrades

You could add:

- Real Pokémon images
- More questions
- A loading animation before the result
- Share button: “I got Pikachu!”
- A random tie-breaker
- A backend to save quiz results
- A React or mobile app version

One note: Pokémon is a Nintendo/Game Freak/The Pokémon Company property, so this is fine as a personal/fan project, but for a public or commercial app you would want to be careful with branding, names, and official artwork.

